{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-513", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/513", "wordCount": 3540, "segments": [{"start": 18.0, "text": "Hi and welcome to session"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "513."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "In this talk you will learn"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "about the lower level details of"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "the new High Efficiency Image"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "File format or HEIF and the many"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "advantages that this new file"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "format standard affords."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "My name is Davide Concion and I"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "manage the Image Compression"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "Team at Apple."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "During the talk, we will briefly"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "touch upon the current de facto"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "standard for image compression,"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "a standard that everybody's"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "familiar with JPEG."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "We will go through the"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "requirements that Apple"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "identified as mandatory for a"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "new image format."}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "We will explain why we think"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "HEIF is the answer to those"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "requirements and we will get to"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "know some of the flexible tools"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "that HEIF implements."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "We will then present the reasons"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "why Apple thinks HEVC is the"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "right codec to be used within"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "the HEIF file format."}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "Let's start with JPEG."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "JPEG is still the most popular"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "compression technology for"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "images only present on the web"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "and on consumer electronics"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "devices, such as the DSLR"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "cameras, point-and-shoot cameras"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "and cell phones."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "Cloud services also use JPEG"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "because of its universal"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "support."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "JPEG though has several"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "limitations, among those are the"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "compression efficiency."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "Several new compression"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "algorithms have been developed"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "in recent years that can shrink"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "the file size much more than"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "JPEG and still maintaining the"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "same objective and subjective"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "quality."}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "Auxiliary images like alpha or"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "depth are not easily supported."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "Also, in recent years new ways"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "to present and display animated"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "images have been developed."}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "Apple Live Photo is one of them."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "JPEG unfortunately does not"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "support animation."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "Let's look at history map of"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "compression standards developed"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "by JPEG and ITU/MPEG."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "JPEG is really starting to show"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "in its years, especially in"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "terms of compression efficiency"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "when compared to recent"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "advancements."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "As you can see in the slide,"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "JPEG has been finalized as a"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "standard in 1992, a quarter of a"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "century ago."}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "Since then, several new"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "compression standards have been"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "developed."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "The latest one in the least is"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "HEVC. And here is HEIF for comparison"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "in the timeline, which has been"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "finalized in 2015."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "Apple invested a lot of time to"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "find a successor for JPEG and"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "many options were evaluated."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "The requirements were extensive."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "The new format needs to support"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "all the features available in"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "JPEG, but at the same time"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "provide better performance."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "It needs to be friendly to"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "professional photography tools,"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "the web and the cloud."}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "The new format also needs to be"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "flexible and extensible to cope"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "with the ever-changing"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "photography ecosystem."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Here is a list of features Apple"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "considered paramount."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "The compression needs to be"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "state-of-the-art both on the"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "front."}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "It needs to be competitive with"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "natural images, but also when"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "compressing text or graphics."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "The format needs to be friendly"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "to hardware accelerated and code"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "and decode operations on modern"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "CPUs, GPUs and ESPs."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "Performance and power is very"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "high in the list of"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "requirements."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "It needs to support high depth"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "and wide color gamut which is"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "the new frontier for images"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "captured on consumer devices."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "It needs to be able to compress"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "4:4:4 color sampling and also"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "describe HDR content, including"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "HDR metadata, transfer function"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "and color space definitions."}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "Auxiliary images for example"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "alpha or depth need to have a"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "commonly defined place in image"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "files."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "New editing tools will be able"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "to utilize auxiliary data for"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "new presentation and editing"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "In recent years, the new ways to"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "present and display animated"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "images have been developed."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "Apple iPhoto is one example."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "Apple iPhoto includes animated"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "content together with static"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "The new common format needs to"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "store animated information"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "efficiently, ideally using"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Tempra compression techniques"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "and be able to instruct players"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "about the presentation intention"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "for example, a looping sequence."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "The new format needs also to"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "support multiple images in the"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "same file."}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "For example, multi-exposure"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "stacks or stereo images."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "This is to aid the development"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "and implementation of new"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "computational photography"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "algorithms."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "Multiple representations of the"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "same image matching the same"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "file are of great importance."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "For example, multi-resolution,"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "including progressively"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "increasing level of details or"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "the ability to represent the"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "same image encoded with"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "different codecs."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "Tiles are an important tool the"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "new format must implement."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "It allows for scalable operation"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "on image of any size."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "We'll be looking into tiles"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "later in the talk."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "The new format needs support for"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "rich metadata associated to each"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "image in the file."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "And also support for time meta"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "for example, a sequence of"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "There is also desire for a new"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "format to be able to include"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "other metadata types for"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "example, audio or text."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "Last but not least, the new"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "format should be flexible and"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "extensible enough to provide a"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "solid foundation for the future."}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "We believe that HEIF is the"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "answer to all these"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "requirements."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "What is HEIF?"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "HEIF stands for High Efficiency"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "Image File Format."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "Version one of the spec became"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "an ISO standard in June of 2015."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "Version two should be released"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "imminently."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "A C reference model for HEIF is"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "available upon request at this"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "link."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "The reference model is meant to"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "provide guidance for HEIF"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "implementation and to understand"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "the specifications."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "As a side note, the open source"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "project GPAC MP4Box has recently"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "added basic functionality to"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "part C files."}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "The vodaworld long time ago"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "learned that containers and"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "codes are different entities and"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "there are several advantages in"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "keeping them separated."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "But historically in the image"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "world containers and codecs are"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "tied together and JPEG is no"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "exception."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "It makes sense to make the"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "distinction in the image world"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "to get the flexibility to"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "."}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "HEIF does exactly that, it"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "specifies a structural format, a"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "container for individual images,"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "as well as image sequences."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "It is built on top of the widely"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "used ISO based media file format"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "which is based on Apple"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "QuickTime technologies."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "It also uses and enhances"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "structures defined in the MP4"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "specification and MPEG-21"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "specifications."}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "Sequences for example, bursts or"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "animations are stored as tracks"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "or time media MP4 style."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "Images coded or derived are"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "stored as items MPEG-21 style."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "Any compression codec can be"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "included in a HEIF container."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "The HEIF specification"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "explicitly mentions HEVC, H264"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "and JPEG in terms of file"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "extensions, types"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "and decoder configuration."}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "The basic building block of a"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "HEIF file like the ISO based"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "media file format is a data"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "structure called box."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "A box is comprised of a"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "four-character type, for"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "instance in the example on the"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "right the ftyp box or the"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "metabox or the mdat box."}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "The size of the box in terms of"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "bytes and the payload of the"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "box."}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "The metabox gives a full"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "description of what is included"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "in the file."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "The handler type of the metabox"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "for whomever is familiar with"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "ISOBMFF specification is of type"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "PICT indicating to a reader that"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "this metabox handles images."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "Before going into the anatomy of"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "a HEIF file a note on file"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "extensions."}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "The standard defines explicitly"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "the file extension of a HEIF"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "file depending on the particular"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "codec being used to compress"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "single images or sequences."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "The list of extensions can be"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "found in the table above."}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "iOS 11 can capture and store"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "HEIF images using the HEVC"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "codec."}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "Therefore, the extension you"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "will be encountering is .HEIC."}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "In iOS 11 and macOS 10.13 we"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "support all three single image"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "HEIF flavors for decoding and"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "displaying."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "Note also that a HEIF file that"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "includes sequences will have a"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "different extension than a HEIF"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "that contains only single"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "We will now dive into the HEIF"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "format and its anatomy."}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "Let's start with the concept of"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "item."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "Every element in a HEIF file is"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "an item."}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "There can be coded items for"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "instance, HEVC encoded frame or"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "tiles."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "There can be derived items for"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "instance, an image overlay or an"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "image grid."}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "There can be metadata items for"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "instance, EXIF, XMP or MPEG-7"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "metadata."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "Each item can also come with"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "several properties associated to"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "Everything is then connected via"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "structures that link certain"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "items to other items or"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "properties."}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "Images are items and because"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "multiple images can be stored in"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "the same file the HEIF standard"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "differentiates between them by"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "assigning certain roles."}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "Some of the roles specified in"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "HEIF are listed in the table"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "above."}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "The primary recovery image is"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "the representative image of a"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "The primary image should be"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "displayed when no other"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "information is possible or"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "decodable by a player."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "Only one primary image can be"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "present in a HEIF file."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Other full-resolution images in"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "HEIF files are called master"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "The thumbnail is a small"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "resolution representation of a"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "master image."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "Multiple thumbnails can be"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "stored in a HEIF for example,"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "with different sizes."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "It's a very useful feature for"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "progressive decoding and"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "displaying very high-resolution"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "The auxiliary image is an image"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "that complements a master image."}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "For example, an alpha plane or a"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "depth map."}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "Auxiliary images can assist in"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "displaying master images, but"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "are not typically displayed."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "A hidden image is an image that"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "should never be displayed."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "It can be present in the file"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "for example, as an input image"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "of a derived image."}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "iOS 11 HEIF implementation uses"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "extensively hidden images which"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "are called tiles."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "Each tile is used to compose the"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "final master or canvas image."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "Now derived manager is an image"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "that is rendered by an indicated"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "operation being performed on"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "other input images."}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "For instance, the canvas image"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "described before is rendered"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "after stitching together"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "multiple tiles."}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "Equivalent images are"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "alternative images for instance,"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "encoded with a different codec."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "A server could distribute the"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "same input content to players"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "that may have different decoding"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "capabilities."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "Once the role has been defined"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "for each image properties can be"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "associated to them."}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "Properties are either"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "descriptive or transformative."}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "They can also be essential for"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "example, the codec"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "initialization info or"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "nonessential."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "The table above provides a"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "non-exhaustive list of"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "descriptive properties for"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "images inside a HEIF file."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "All the usual suspect"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "information can be found in"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "there like the image size, the"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "color information, the type of"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "auxiliary image which can be"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "alpha or depth and also the"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "configuration parameters to"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "initialize the decoder."}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "The table above provides a"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "non-exhaustive list of"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "transformative properties."}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "The presence of these properties"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "instructs a HEIF"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "that the image needs to go"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "through extra steps before being"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "displayed."}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "For example, the clean aperture"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "property instructs a HEIF reader"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "that the crop operation must be"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "performed before rending the"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "final image."}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "All the properties for each"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "image are grouped together in"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "the same item property box."}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "Each image can then be"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "associated to which property via"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "the association box."}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "We will use an example to"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "describe how the association"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "works."}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "The above HEIF container on the"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "left describes the file with one"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "main image and one thumbnail."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "The main image is comprised of"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "four tiles."}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "The item property box or ipco"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "box contains all the decoder"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "configuration and the sizes of"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "the main image, the tiles and"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "the thumbnails."}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "Note that the order matters for"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "this box."}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "The association box or ipma box"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "on the right groups properties"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "nicely based on their position"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "with the item ID in the file."}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "As explained before, there is a"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "total of six items in the file,"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "one image, four tiles and one"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "thumbnail."}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "Items 1 through 4 are the tiles,"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "these are hidden images with"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "properties in position one, the"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "decoder configuration and"}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "position two, the size which is"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "500 by 500 pixel."}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "Item five is the main image,"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "only the size property is"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "defined since this is this is a"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "derived image."}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "The size is 1,000 by 1,000"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "pixels."}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "Next, we will briefly talk about"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "image sequences in HEIF."}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "When sequences are embedded in a"}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "HEIF file the move box and it's"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "sub boxes are also present in"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "the file."}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "The move boxes fully described"}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "in the ISO MP4 file format"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "specification from which HEIF"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "derives."}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "Each sequence of images or"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "samples is described via the"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "trak box where all the timing"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "information to play back the"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "track is included."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "HEIF specifies a new track"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "handler for picture called pict."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "The key difference is that while"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "the timing information given for"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "a video or an audio track is"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "used to synchronize the playback"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "the timing information an image"}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "sequence track can represent"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "either the capture time for"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "example, a burst or the"}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "suggested display time for"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "example, to derive a slideshow."}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "Roles can be used for image"}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "sequences to."}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "For example, a HEIF file could"}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "embed a track of thumbnails or a"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "track of auxiliary images"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "associated with the master"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "track."}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "One of the most important HEIF"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "features is the ability to"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "control the playback by"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "signaling in the file the intent"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "of the creator."}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "For example, an edit list"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "enables modifying the playback"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "order and pace of each sample."}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "HEIF also allows indicating edit"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "list repetitions for example,"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "for looping animations."}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "The repetition can be indicated"}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "to last for a certain duration"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "or be infinite."}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "Given that the ISO tracks can be"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "used in HEIF files interframe"}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "prediction is also available."}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "Inter prediction is the ability"}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "to remove coded information by"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "predicting the content of the"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "current frame from similar"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "frames in the past or in the"}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "future."}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "This gives a tremendous"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "advantage in terms of"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "compression."}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "Inter prediction can also"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "introduce a delay decode time"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "because the previous frames must"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "be decoded first before being"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "able to decode the current"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "frame."}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "HEIF allows inter prediction,"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "but also includes constraints in"}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "the file to limit frame"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "interdependencies."}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "For instance, each predicted"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "image can be restricted to point"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "only to unknown predicted image"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "or inter."}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "In this case, the time to decode"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "each frame in a sequence becomes"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "deterministic."}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "Last but not least, a HEIF image"}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "can be subdivided into tiles."}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "Tiles are rectangular regions"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "within an image."}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "They are completely independent"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "items in a HEIF file and they"}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "can be of different or same"}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "size."}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "If their size is different a"}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "relative location property"}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "describes their position in the"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "final image."}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "If their size is the same the"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "final image is described as a"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "grid. Several reasons why tiles"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "make HEIF extremely flexible."}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "A player can exploit parallelism"}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "and decode time."}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "For example, each tile can be"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "separately and independently"}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "decoded."}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "Tiles can be used to reduce"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "memory consumption when resizing"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "an image rather than decoding"}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "the whole much and then apply a"}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "rescale operation each tile can"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "be independently decoded and"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "rescaled and then placed in a"}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "smaller buffer for rendering."}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "Cropping becomes very fast"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "because a player does not need"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "to decode the whole image to"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "extract a certain region."}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "This property is extremely"}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "useful for zooming operation."}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "For instance, a gigapixel image"}, {"start": 1200.0, "text": "could be decoded and displayed"}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "and zoomed in with ease without"}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "the need to decode the whole"}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "image into a multi gigabit"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "buffer. Of note, the tiles can be used"}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "also as an encoding tool."}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "A smart encoder can make"}, {"start": 1218.0, "text": "different decision based on the"}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "content of each tile."}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "Apple HEIF implementation uses"}, {"start": 1226.0, "text": "tiles extensively."}, {"start": 1228.0, "text": "Note though that the HEVC"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "specification also supports"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "subdividing a frame into tiles"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "as a parallelization tool."}, {"start": 1236.0, "text": "Apple does not use tiles in HEVC"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "parlance, but rather each tile"}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "is a whole HEVC frame, we call"}, {"start": 1244.0, "text": "them system tiles."}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "Next, we will talk about HEVC,"}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "the codec Apple has chosen to"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "compress HEIF photos."}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "Two of the major reasons for"}, {"start": 1259.0, "text": "selecting HEVC."}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "First, HEVC is the latest"}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "technology in the compression"}, {"start": 1265.0, "text": "standard world."}, {"start": 1267.0, "text": "With HEVC we see an average of"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "2X compression compared to JPEG"}, {"start": 1272.0, "text": "containing the same visual"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "quality."}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "Second, HEVC hardware support is"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "becoming available in most CPUs"}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "and GPUs."}, {"start": 1280.0, "text": "For instance, HEVC hardware"}, {"start": 1282.0, "text": "support is available from the"}, {"start": 1284.0, "text": "sixth generation Intel core"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "processors."}, {"start": 1287.0, "text": "This means except means"}, {"start": 1289.0, "text": "exceptional performance without"}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "sacrificing battery life."}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "Several inter coding tools have"}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "been added to the standard that"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "allow HEVC to outperform JPEG."}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "In the next few slides we will"}, {"start": 1304.0, "text": "mention some."}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "You will notice that the common"}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "theme here is flexibility."}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "First, the block size."}, {"start": 1314.0, "text": "JPEG divides each image into a"}, {"start": 1317.0, "text": "grid of blocks of 8 by 8 pixels."}, {"start": 1320.0, "text": "These blocks are then described"}, {"start": 1323.0, "text": "transformed and quantized."}, {"start": 1326.0, "text": "HEVC has the flexibility of"}, {"start": 1329.0, "text": "being able to divide an image in"}, {"start": 1331.0, "text": "blocks that are 64 by 64 pixels"}, {"start": 1334.0, "text": "down to 4 by 4 pixels."}, {"start": 1337.0, "text": "The transform size is also"}, {"start": 1339.0, "text": "flexible within the block."}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "A new optional discrete"}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "transform has been"}, {"start": 1344.0, "text": "added to the standard and three"}, {"start": 1346.0, "text": "possible scanning orders are"}, {"start": 1348.0, "text": "available to group coded"}, {"start": 1349.0, "text": "coefficients."}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "Next, the block prediction."}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "JPEG allows the top left corner"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "coefficient also called the DC"}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "component or the constant"}, {"start": 1360.0, "text": "component of an 8 by 8 block to"}, {"start": 1363.0, "text": "be predicted from the block on"}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "the left."}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "HEVC adds the flexibility to"}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "predict every pixel value within"}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "a block. Up to 35 angular predictions are"}, {"start": 1374.0, "text": "available."}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "Being able to remove redundant"}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "information in a block by"}, {"start": 1379.0, "text": "exploiting similar information"}, {"start": 1381.0, "text": "available in neighboring blocks"}, {"start": 1382.0, "text": "is one of the most efficient"}, {"start": 1384.0, "text": "tools inside HEVC."}, {"start": 1387.0, "text": "Entropy coding."}, {"start": 1389.0, "text": "JPEG uses Huffman coding as the"}, {"start": 1391.0, "text": "engine for statistical encoding."}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "The idea is to assign variable"}, {"start": 1395.0, "text": "length codes to input"}, {"start": 1397.0, "text": "coefficient."}, {"start": 1399.0, "text": "With shorter length codes"}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "assigned to coefficients with"}, {"start": 1403.0, "text": "higher frequency."}, {"start": 1405.0, "text": "HEVC on the other hand, employs"}, {"start": 1408.0, "text": "an arithmetic coder called CABAC"}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "which stands for Context"}, {"start": 1412.0, "text": "Adaptive Binary Arithmetic"}, {"start": 1414.0, "text": "Coding. CABAC is notable for providing"}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "much better compression than"}, {"start": 1419.0, "text": "most other entropy encoding"}, {"start": 1421.0, "text": "algorithms."}, {"start": 1424.0, "text": "Quantization."}, {"start": 1426.0, "text": "Quantization is a C"}, {"start": 1428.0, "text": "compression technique achieved"}, {"start": 1430.0, "text": "by compressing a range of values"}, {"start": 1433.0, "text": "to a single quantum value."}, {"start": 1435.0, "text": "JPEG utilizes global"}, {"start": 1437.0, "text": "quantization matrixes for each 8"}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "by 8 block."}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "HEVC on top of the quantization"}, {"start": 1444.0, "text": "matrix adds the flexibility of"}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "assigning a different"}, {"start": 1448.0, "text": "quantization parameter for each"}, {"start": 1450.0, "text": "block."}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "This allows smart encoding"}, {"start": 1452.0, "text": "algorithms to compress more"}, {"start": 1455.0, "text": "areas of an image while the"}, {"start": 1457.0, "text": "human visual system is less"}, {"start": 1458.0, "text": "susceptible to detect artifacts."}, {"start": 1462.0, "text": "For instance, high-frequency"}, {"start": 1463.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 1464.0, "text": "Next is the blocking, a tool"}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "that is available only in HEVC."}, {"start": 1471.0, "text": "Blocking artifacts are visible"}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "discontinuities occurring at"}, {"start": 1475.0, "text": "block boundaries."}, {"start": 1476.0, "text": "The HEVC deblocking filter is a"}, {"start": 1479.0, "text": "filter applied to the pixels"}, {"start": 1482.0, "text": "around the block edges to"}, {"start": 1484.0, "text": "smoothen the transition and get"}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "more pleasing visual results."}, {"start": 1489.0, "text": "SAO which stands for Sample"}, {"start": 1491.0, "text": "Adaptive Offset is an extra"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "filtering step available in HEVC"}, {"start": 1497.0, "text": "that is applied to the output of"}, {"start": 1499.0, "text": "the deblocking filter to further"}, {"start": 1501.0, "text": "improve the quality."}, {"start": 1503.0, "text": "It's a local filter that can"}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "attenuate bringing artifacts or"}, {"start": 1508.0, "text": "changes in sample intensity of"}, {"start": 1509.0, "text": "some areas of a picture for a"}, {"start": 1511.0, "text": "better visual quality."}, {"start": 1514.0, "text": "Both these techniques allow for"}, {"start": 1517.0, "text": "more pleasing images, especially"}, {"start": 1519.0, "text": "when the compression is very"}, {"start": 1520.0, "text": "high."}, {"start": 1522.0, "text": "We have gone through several"}, {"start": 1523.0, "text": "HEIF and HEVC features and"}, {"start": 1525.0, "text": "tools, I wanted to take a second"}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "to mention a few characteristics"}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "of HEIF files captured on iOS"}, {"start": 1532.0, "text": "11."}, {"start": 1533.0, "text": "First, the extension for HEIF"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "images captured with iOS 11 will"}, {"start": 1539.0, "text": "be .HEIC because of the HEVC"}, {"start": 1542.0, "text": "codec."}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "The HEVC profile utilized to"}, {"start": 1546.0, "text": "compress images is the main"}, {"start": 1548.0, "text": "still profile."}, {"start": 1550.0, "text": "Also, we use HEVC monochrome"}, {"start": 1553.0, "text": "profile for depth data."}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "Images are encoded using tiles"}, {"start": 1559.0, "text": "that are 512 by 512 pixels."}, {"start": 1563.0, "text": "They are positioned in a grid"}, {"start": 1565.0, "text": "fashion to cover the whole"}, {"start": 1567.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 1568.0, "text": "The thumbnail is a 320 by 240"}, {"start": 1571.0, "text": "image HEVC encoded."}, {"start": 1575.0, "text": "It is four times the size of a"}, {"start": 1577.0, "text": "common 160 by 120 JPEG thumbnail"}, {"start": 1580.0, "text": "and this is to help showing"}, {"start": 1582.0, "text": "better thumbnail quality when"}, {"start": 1584.0, "text": "images are displayed on modern"}, {"start": 1586.0, "text": "screens with high pixel density."}, {"start": 1589.0, "text": "EXIF metadata is part of the"}, {"start": 1591.0, "text": "HEIF file like JPEG for backward"}, {"start": 1594.0, "text": "compatibility."}, {"start": 1596.0, "text": "Depth data is stored as an"}, {"start": 1599.0, "text": "auxiliary image and the metadata"}, {"start": 1602.0, "text": "pertinent to depth is stored as"}, {"start": 1604.0, "text": "XMP payload associated with the"}, {"start": 1607.0, "text": "depth image."}, {"start": 1608.0, "text": "Last, a note about file"}, {"start": 1612.0, "text": "creation."}, {"start": 1614.0, "text": "The HEIF standard does not"}, {"start": 1616.0, "text": "mandate any order for the boxes"}, {"start": 1619.0, "text": "a reader could find at the top"}, {"start": 1620.0, "text": "level of a HEIF file, but we"}, {"start": 1622.0, "text": "found that ordering them in a"}, {"start": 1624.0, "text": "certain way greatly helps"}, {"start": 1626.0, "text": "parsers and decoders."}, {"start": 1628.0, "text": "For example, having the"}, {"start": 1630.0, "text": "thumbnail early in the file"}, {"start": 1631.0, "text": "would allow parsing and display"}, {"start": 1634.0, "text": "huge amount of HEIF images"}, {"start": 1635.0, "text": "without the need to parse the"}, {"start": 1637.0, "text": "whole file."}, {"start": 1639.0, "text": "For transmission or"}, {"start": 1641.0, "text": "web application once the metabox"}, {"start": 1643.0, "text": "is received all the information"}, {"start": 1646.0, "text": "for the file is available and"}, {"start": 1647.0, "text": "therefore readers can start"}, {"start": 1649.0, "text": "configuring the decoding and"}, {"start": 1651.0, "text": "display pipelines before having"}, {"start": 1654.0, "text": "received the whole coded data."}, {"start": 1662.0, "text": "Let's summarize what we have"}, {"start": 1664.0, "text": "learned today."}, {"start": 1665.0, "text": "The photography world needs a"}, {"start": 1667.0, "text": "better image file format to"}, {"start": 1669.0, "text": "replace the rather old JPEG."}, {"start": 1671.0, "text": "We looked at the extensive list"}, {"start": 1675.0, "text": "of requirements that Apple"}, {"start": 1678.0, "text": "considered paramount when"}, {"start": 1679.0, "text": "searching for a JPEG"}, {"start": 1681.0, "text": "replacement."}, {"start": 1682.0, "text": "We believe HEIF is the answer"}, {"start": 1686.0, "text": "for all the requirements."}, {"start": 1688.0, "text": "Its flexibility allows to handle"}, {"start": 1690.0, "text": "with ease and elegance the"}, {"start": 1692.0, "text": "advancements available in iOS 11"}, {"start": 1695.0, "text": "and its extensibility also"}, {"start": 1697.0, "text": "allows HEIF to be a solid"}, {"start": 1699.0, "text": "foundation for the future."}, {"start": 1701.0, "text": "We then analyzed the various"}, {"start": 1703.0, "text": "features available in the HEIF"}, {"start": 1705.0, "text": "standard."}, {"start": 1707.0, "text": "And finally, we looked at the"}, {"start": 1709.0, "text": "HEVC tools that make it the best"}, {"start": 1711.0, "text": "choice, both in terms of"}, {"start": 1713.0, "text": "compression efficiency and"}, {"start": 1715.0, "text": "friendliness toward hardware"}, {"start": 1717.0, "text": "architecture for performance and"}, {"start": 1719.0, "text": "power."}, {"start": 1720.0, "text": "For more information, please"}, {"start": 1723.0, "text": "visit the URL for the High"}, {"start": 1726.0, "text": "Efficiency Image File format"}, {"start": 1728.0, "text": "session 513."}, {"start": 1731.0, "text": "And if you're still at the show"}, {"start": 1733.0, "text": "we invite you to visit the two"}, {"start": 1735.0, "text": "related sessions about HEIF and"}, {"start": 1738.0, "text": "HEVC."}, {"start": 1739.0, "text": "Thank you for watching the talk"}]}
